***************************** T A L Y S **************************1425 1451  187
                                                                  1425 1451  188
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   1425 1451  189
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      1425 1451  190
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    1425 1451  191
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     1425 1451  192
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  1425 1451  193
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        1425 1451  194
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    1425 1451  195
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         1425 1451  196
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      1425 1451  197
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    1425 1451  198
stored in this data file:                                         1425 1451  199
                                                                  1425 1451  200
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   1425 1451  201
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     1425 1451  202
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 1425 1451  203
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   1425 1451  204
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                1425 1451  205
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   1425 1451  206
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    1425 1451  207
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        1425 1451  208
- Recoil data                                                     1425 1451  209
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           1425 1451  210
- Total particle energy spectra                                   1425 1451  211
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      1425 1451  212
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        1425 1451  213
- Residual production cross sections                              1425 1451  214
                                                                  1425 1451  215
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            1425 1451  216
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        1425 1451  217
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   1425 1451  218
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                1425 1451  219
                                                                  1425 1451  220
***************** F I L E   I N F O R M A T I O N ****************1425 1451  221
                                                                  1425 1451  222
##### MF1: GENERAL INFORMATION                                    1425 1451  223
                                                                  1425 1451  224
- MT451    : Descriptive data and directory                       1425 1451  225
                                                                  1425 1451  226
This text and the full directory of used MF/MT sections.          1425 1451  227
                                                                  1425 1451  228
##### MF2: RESONANCE PARAMETERS                                   1425 1451  229
                                                                  1425 1451  230
- MT151    : Resonance parameters                                 1425 1451  231
                                                                  1425 1451  232
Details about the origin of the resonance parameters for this     1425 1451  233
nuclide are given above in this description. In general, both a   1425 1451  234
Resolved and an Unresolved Resonance Range are given.             1425 1451  235
                                                                  1425 1451  236
##### MF3: REACTION CROSS SECTIONS                                1425 1451  237
                                                                  1425 1451  238
All the data present in the following MT-sections have been       1425 1451  239
calculated with TALYS, possibly normalized to experimental data.  1425 1451  240
If the maximal cross section in an excitation function over the   1425 1451  241
whole energy range does not exceed 1.e-9 b, the MT-number is not  1425 1451  242
included. Cross sections lower than 1.e-20 b are assumed to have  1425 1451  243
no physical meaning and are set to zero. All MT numbers extend up 1425 1451  244
to the highest incident energy.                                   1425 1451  245
The following reaction channels/MT numbers are generally included:1425 1451  246
                                                                  1425 1451  247
- MT1      : Total cross section                                  1425 1451  248
                                                                  1425 1451  249
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range,    1425 1451  250
or partly reproduced using experimental data.                     1425 1451  251
                                                                  1425 1451  252
- MT2      : Elastic scattering cross section                     1425 1451  253
                                                                  1425 1451  254
Obtained by subtracting the non-elastic cross section from the    1425 1451  255
total cross section.                                              1425 1451  256
                                                                  1425 1451  257
- MT3      : Non-elastic cross section                            1425 1451  258
                                                                  1425 1451  259
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range.    1425 1451  260
                                                                  1425 1451  261
- MT4      : Total inelastic cross section                        1425 1451  262
                                                                  1425 1451  263
Sum of MT=51-91.                                                  1425 1451  264
                                                                  1425 1451  265
- MT5      : (n,anything) cross section                           1425 1451  266
                                                                  1425 1451  267
MT5 contains the reactions which can not be stored in any other   1425 1451  268
MT-number. The information of MF3/MT5 can be combined with        1425 1451  269
MF6/MT5 to obtain residual production cross sections particle     1425 1451  270
production cross sections and (double-)differential cross         1425 1451  271
sections.                                                         1425 1451  272
                                                                  1425 1451  273
- MT16     : (n,2n) cross section                                 1425 1451  274
- MT17     : (n,3n) cross section                                 1425 1451  275
- MT22     : (n,na) cross section                                 1425 1451  276
- MT28     : (n,np) cross section                                 1425 1451  277
- MT51-90  : (n,n') cross section for 1st-40th excited state      1425 1451  278
- MT91     : (n,n') continuum cross section                       1425 1451  279
- MT102    : (n,gamma) cross section                              1425 1451  280
- MT103    : (n,p) cross section                                  1425 1451  281
- MT104    : (n,d) cross section                                  1425 1451  282
- MT105    : (n,t) cross section                                  1425 1451  283
- MT106    : (n,h) cross section                                  1425 1451  284
- MT107    : (n,a) cross section                                  1425 1451  285
- MT600-610: (n,p) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       1425 1451  286
- MT649    : (n,p) continuum cross section                        1425 1451  287
- MT650-655: (n,d) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        1425 1451  288
- MT699    : (n,d) continuum cross section                        1425 1451  289
- MT700-705: (n,t) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        1425 1451  290
- MT749    : (n,t) continuum cross section                        1425 1451  291
- MT750-755: (n,h) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        1425 1451  292
- MT799    : (n,h) continuum cross section                        1425 1451  293
- MT800-810: (n,a) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       1425 1451  294
- MT849    : (n,a) continuum cross section                        1425 1451  295
                                                                  1425 1451  296
##### MF4: ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS OF SECONDARY PARTICLES           1425 1451  297
                                                                  1425 1451  298
We use MF4 for the neutron scattering angular distribution for    1425 1451  299
discrete levels.                                                  1425 1451  300
                                                                  1425 1451  301
- MT2      : Elastic angular distribution                         1425 1451  302
                                                                  1425 1451  303
The flag LTT=3 is used to indicate a switch at some high energy,  1425 1451  304
generally 50 MeV, from a Legendre representation to a tabulated   1425 1451  305
representation. For incident energies below this energy, the      1425 1451  306
Legendre coefficients are given on a sufficiently precise energy  1425 1451  307
grid. They are a sum of calculated Legendre coefficients for      1425 1451  308
compound nucleus and shape-elastic scattering. For higher         1425 1451  309
incident energies, relative angular distributions are tabulated   1425 1451  310
on an angular grid.                                               1425 1451  311
                                                                  1425 1451  312
- MT51-70  : (n,n') angular distribution for 1st-20th state       1425 1451  313
- MT600-610: (n,p) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        1425 1451  314
- MT650-655: (n,d) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         1425 1451  315
- MT700-705: (n,t) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         1425 1451  316
- MT750-755: (n,h) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         1425 1451  317
- MT800-810: (n,a) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        1425 1451  318
                                                                  1425 1451  319
##### MF6: PRODUCT ENERGY-ANGLE DISTRIBUTIONS                     1425 1451  320
                                                                  1425 1451  321
In MF6 we store all secondary energy, angle, and energy-angle     1425 1451  322
distributions, as well as all residual and discrete + continuum   1425 1451  323
photon production cross sections for channels other than capture  1425 1451  324
(MT102) and reactions to discrete levels (MT51,etc.).             1425 1451  325
All data are generated with TALYS.                                1425 1451  326
                                                                  1425 1451  327
- MT5      : (n,anything) yields and energy-angle distributions   1425 1451  328
                                                                  1425 1451  329
MT5 contains, in this order,                                      1425 1451  330
For neutrons up to alpha particles and photons:                   1425 1451  331
- the production yields per particle for the whole energy range   1425 1451  332
- the secondary energy-angle distributions per particles which are1425 1451  333
  not represented by explicit MT numbers. On a secondary energy   1425 1451  334
  grid the relative emission spectra are given together with the  1425 1451  335
  parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular              1425 1451  336
  distributions. Inelastic scattering cross sections for discrete 1425 1451  337
  states have been broadened and added to the continuum spectra.  1425 1451  338
For each residual product:                                        1425 1451  339
- the production yields for the whole energy range.               1425 1451  340
- the recoil                                                      1425 1451  341
These distributions can be multiplied with MF3/MT5 to get         1425 1451  342
the production cross sections and (double-)differential cross     1425 1451  343
sections.                                                         1425 1451  344
                                                                  1425 1451  345
- MT16     : (n,2n) energy-angle distr. and photon production     1425 1451  346
                                                                  1425 1451  347
First, for each type of outgoing particle, the (trivial) integer  1425 1451  348
particle yields are given. Next, on a sufficiently dense incident 1425 1451  349
energy grid the secondary energy-angle distributions are          1425 1451  350
specified by means of the relative emission spectra and the       1425 1451  351
parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular distributions. 1425 1451  352
Next, the photon yield is tabulated as a function of incident     1425 1451  353
energy. For each incident energy, the photon production is given  1425 1451  354
for all discrete gamma lines present in the final nucleus. A      1425 1451  355
continuum photon distribution is added to this. We assume         1425 1451  356
isotropy for all produced gamma rays.                             1425 1451  357
                                                                  1425 1451  358
For the following MT-numbers, the same procedure as for MT16 is   1425 1451  359
followed:                                                         1425 1451  360
                                                                  1425 1451  361
- MT17 : (n,3n) energy-angle distr. and photon production         1425 1451  362
- MT22 : (n,na) energy-angle distr. and photon production         1425 1451  363
- MT28 : (n,np) energy-angle distr. and photon production         1425 1451  364
- MT91 : (n,n') continuum energy-angle distr. and phot. prod.     1425 1451  365
- MT649: (n,p) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     1425 1451  366
- MT699: (n,d) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     1425 1451  367
- MT749: (n,t) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     1425 1451  368
- MT809: (n,h) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     1425 1451  369
- MT849: (n,a) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     1425 1451  370
                                                                  1425 1451  371
##### MF8: RADIOACTIVE DECAY DATA                                 1425 1451  372
                                                                  1425 1451  373
For reactions to isomers, MF8 designates where the information    1425 1451  374
for isomeric versus ground state production, or residual          1425 1451  375
production can be found, i.e. for each MT number it points to     1425 1451  376
either MF6, MF9 or MF10.                                          1425 1451  377
                                                                  1425 1451  378
##### MF9: MULTIPLICITIES FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES  1425 1451  379
                                                                  1425 1451  380
MF9 is used for isomer production by non-threshold reactions.     1425 1451  381
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    1425 1451  382
as isomer.                                                        1425 1451  383
                                                                  1425 1451  384
##### MF10: CROSS SECTIONS FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES 1425 1451  385
                                                                  1425 1451  386
MF10 is used for isomer production by threshold reactions.        1425 1451  387
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    1425 1451  388
as isomer.                                                        1425 1451  389
                                                                  1425 1451  390
##### MF12: PHOTON PRODUCTION YIELD DATA                          1425 1451  391
                                                                  1425 1451  392
MF12 is used for the photon production for two types of reactions:1425 1451  393
- Reactions to discrete levels (MT51, etc.) For this transition   1425 1451  394
  probabilities are used (LO=2)                                   1425 1451  395
- Photons from neutron capture (MT102). Here multiplicities are   1425 1451  396
  given                                                           1425 1451  397
                                                                  1425 1451  398
##### MF14: PHOTON ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                          1425 1451  399
                                                                  1425 1451  400
All photon production is considered as isotropic                  1425 1451  401
                                                                  1425 1451  402
##### MF15: PHOTON ENERGY SPECTRA                                 1425 1451  403
                                                                  1425 1451  404
For capture (MT102), the photon energy spectrum is given.         1425 1451  405
                                                                  1425 1451  406
##### MF32: COVARIANCES OF RESONANCE PARAMETERS                   1425 1451  407
                                                                  1425 1451  408
In MF32, we store the covariances of resonance parameters,        1425 1451  409
and more details are given above in this description. In most     1425 1451  410
versions of TENDL, this information is now stored in MF33.        1425 1451  411
                                                                  1425 1451  412
##### MF33: COVARIANCES OF NEUTRON CROSS SECTIONS                 1425 1451  413
                                                                  1425 1451  414
In MF33, we store the covariances of most, but not all, reaction  1425 1451  415
channels that are given in MF3. All covariances are generated     1425 1451  416
with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates TALYS runs using    1425 1451  417
a Monte Carlo parameter method.                                   1425 1451  418
For each MT-number, the information consists of:                  1425 1451  419
1. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Ea (variances)                1425 1451  420
2. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Eb (correlations for the      1425 1451  421
   same reaction channel between different energies)              1425 1451  422
3. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Ea (correlations between      1425 1451  423
   different reaction channels for the same energy)               1425 1451  424
4. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Eb (correlations between      1425 1451  425
   different reaction channels for different energies)            1425 1451  426
Classes 1 and 2 are covered by NI-type subsubsections with        1425 1451  427
flag LB=5, followed by a LB=8 section which contains              1425 1451  428
the cross section variances multiplied by 1.e-3. Next, classes 3  1425 1451  429
and 4 are covered by flag LB=6 to account for the different       1425 1451  430
energy grids that two correlating MT-sections may have. Since     1425 1451  431
the total correlation matrix is fully symmetric, we only need to  1425 1451  432
include the correlation elements between different MT-numbers     1425 1451  433
once, and we do that in the subsection with the lowest of the     1425 1451  434
two MT-numbers. We include covariance information for all the     1425 1451  435
total cross sections, the lumped partial cross sections and the   1425 1451  436
individual inelastic cross sections per level (MT51,...). We do   1425 1451  437
not include covariances for MT600 and higher MT-numbers. For the  1425 1451  438
most important channels, we include cross-channel correlations.   1425 1451  439
                                                                  1425 1451  440
##### MF34: COVARIANCES OF ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                  1425 1451  441
                                                                  1425 1451  442
In MF34, we store the covariances of the elastic scattering       1425 1451  443
angular distributions that are given in MF4/MT2. All covariances  1425 1451  444
are generated with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates       1425 1451  445
TALYS runs using a Monte Carlo parameter method. The tables are   1425 1451  446
restricted to MT2 and contain covariances for the first 6         1425 1451  447
Legendre coefficients. Both intra- and inter-correlations of the  1425 1451  448
various Legendre coefficients are given. As in MF33, the LB5      1425 1451  449
representation is used.                                           1425 1451  450
                                                                  1425 1451  451
##### MF40: COVARIANCES OF ISOMER PRODUCTION                      1425 1451  452
                                                                  1425 1451  453
For covariances of ground state and isomeric cross sections, the  1425 1451  454
same procedures as for MF33 are used.                             1425 1451  455
                                                                  1425 1451  456
